<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murad II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1404">1404</a>–1451</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Murad II was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from 1421 to 1451, with a brief abdication in 1444 to 1446. He restored Ottoman power after the civil war that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s victory, inherited the Germiyanid lands in 1429, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1430, and defeated crusading armies at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> in 1444 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> in 1448. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murad-ii.jpg" alt="Murad II" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1584-1588 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murad_II._H%C3%BCnername,_folio_143b._TSMK_Hazine_1523_(created_1584-1588).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
